"_note": "Filament paths in BoxTurtle CAD coordinates (mm), by tools/hub_paths.py. Lanes are numbered by X, lane1 lowest. Each fitting socket and the PTFE counterbore behind it are coaxial: their axis is fitted through the mid-points of both in a section of the hub body at the plane of the outlet axis. Every ECAS04 collet is set on that axis (turned by angle about the point about, moved to, dz), at its CAD distance from the socket floor; the load-only hub, which has no fittings in its STEP, gets the combo's inlet collets and the v1.0 hub's outlet collet. PTFE is inferred: coaxial with the fitting and inserted to the shoulder where the counterbore steps down to the filament channel (lanes: seat; outlet: shoulder). Each lane path starts there and follows its own channel: the channels are swept cylinders, so each wall face stepped inward by the bore radius lands on its channel centre line, and the path walks those points to the outlet axis (X 150.1).",
